## Back on the island

The [browser version](https://khawkins98.github.io/johnny_web/) offers Classic and Enhanced playback. Classic keeps the native 320×200 scale, static clouds and original waves; Enhanced adds responsive scaling with animated clouds and ocean waves. The original Dynamix and Sierra pixel art, audio cues, and gags remain the center of the experience.

To run it, you provide the original game data. The [README](https://github.com/khawkins98/johnny_web#readme) links the floppy archive; dropping its ZIP or extracted `.ima` disk image directly onto the page imports the resources into browser storage.

Like my [recent Mac OS 9 work](/posts/20260810-newsheep-sheepshaver-mac-os-9-2-apple-silicon-jit/), this started with wanting to spend time with vintage software again. Johnny's small island turned out to contain a surprisingly sophisticated simulation engine that was a joy to unpack.

I'd love to hear which gag you remember, or where you first saw him. It is great having that little castaway back at work in the corner of a screen.

